            <node unique_id="1198" master_id="0" name="Wordbridger_6" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
              <rich_text>Worldbridger.6
   Path: \Musing of the Meaning\Humanmetrics\Astrology\Mayan\White\)
Leaf 1:
http://www.mayantimes.com/White%20Worldbridger.htm
Challenge: Yellow Warrior
Occult: Blue Eagle
Guide: 
Like-minded: Red Skywalker
Birth Glyph: White Worldbridger


Leaf 2:

The White Worldbridger is the sixth glyph and it represents `death and equality`. It is the diplomat of the Tzolkin. In order to bridge the worlds between where we are now and where we could be, we first of all need to build a bridge. But this entails a process of death. To go forth one must let go of parts of the old self which have no place. All the things that hold you back, the part of you that is no longer relevant, must be released. This is why death and equality are key words for White Worldbridger. People born on these days are often diplomatic and they strive to find ways to bring together people of opposing views. They seek peace in the world. We all have within ourselves two different places, The place where we go to dream and to ponder where there is peace and tranquility. Where we can travel to other worlds and fantasise . The other part of our mind is grounded on the earth and concerned with paying bills and making ends meet and surviving on the physical plane. These two parts are connected via a bridge. There must however be a balance between these two places, never should you reside more in one than the other. These issues will always affect people born on White Worldbridger days. The shaman in order to obtain understanding of life must first of all allow his ego to die. The shamans death is the death of his own self importance. To cross bridges into other worlds, to expand your mind you must first let go of the identity that
separates you from the rest of the world.

All people born on White Worldbridger days have in common in their birth chart the same challenge, occult and like-minded glyphs. Only the guide changes and that is because the guide is decided according to what your number is.

The challenge of the White Worldbridger is the Yellow Warrior. This glyph symbolises `questing and intelligence`. A challenge is given to someone in order to measure their worth. When you overcome a challenge then you reach your personal potential. Many people are held back in their lives because they fail to overcome their challenge. It is what makes us strong. For the White Worldbridger to have the Yellow Warrior as a challenge suggests that the the worldbridger needs ask more questions and find their quest. Until they succeed in becoming a warrior they will not succeed in bridging the worlds.

The occult glyph for the White Worldbridger is the Blue Eagle. This glyph symbolises `creativity and vision`. The occult glyph represents the magical gift that you have to help you on your mission in life. The Blue Eagle sees things from a higher perspective, therefore to have it in a magical position as the occult means that White Worldbridger can see the world of a magic from the eagles eye point of view.
This makes them very open minded. Creativity is your secret weapon.

The like-minded glyph for the White Worldbridger is the Red Skywalker. This glyph represents `courage and exploring`. The like-minded glyph in a birth chart symbolises your ally. Out of all the other glyphs in the Tzolkin, you have more in common with the Red Skywalker then any of the others. When ever you get together you will feel the connection.

Challenge
White Mirror

Like Minded
Blue Monkey

Occult
White Mirror

Guide
  	  	 
White magnetic Worldbridger
	66 	White Worldbridger
White Lunar Worldbridger
	106 	White Mirror
White Electric Worldbridger
	146 	White Dog
White self existing Worldbridger
	186 	White Wind
White Overtone Worldbridger
	226 	White Wizard
White Rhythmic Worldbridger
	6 	White Worldbridger
White Resonant Worldbridger
	46 	White Mirror
White Galactic Worldbridger
	86 	White Dog
White Solar Worldbridger
	126 	White Wind
White Planetary Worldbridger
	166 	White Wizard
White Spectral Worldbridger
	206 	White Worldbridger
White Crystal Worldbridger
	246 	White Mirror
White Cosmic Worldbridger
	26 	White Dog

If you were born on a number one (magnetic) day or on a number six (rhythmic) day or a number eleven (spectral) day , then you are guided by the White Worldbridger. Or another way of saying it is that you are guided by your own power doubled. People who are guided by themselves are self-reliant, resourceful and often stubborn. This can lead to frustration sometimes as when you would like to find the answer to a problem no one ever gives it to you. You always have to figure everything out for yourself.

If you are born on a number two (lunar) or a number seven (resonant) or a number twelve (crystal) then you are guided by the
White Mirror. This glyph represents reflecting truth. For a White Worldbridger to be guided by the influence of the White Mirror entails showing people the truth in order for them to cross bridges. Clarity and truth are vital in order to enable your mind to travel to other worlds. Know thyself and then you shall know the universe.

If you are born on a number three (electric) or a number eight (galactic) or a number thirteen (cosmic), then you are guided by the
White Dog. This glyph symbolises `love loyalty and heart`. For a White Worldbridger to be guided by a White Dog means that your mission in life is to show people love. You are not only motivated to find peace and be that diplomat but you are motivated to show
people that all you need is love.

If you are born on a number four (self-existing) day or on a number nine (solar) day then you are guided by the White Wind. This glyph represents communication and spirit. It is the messagener of the Tzolkin. To be guided by White Wind is to be guided by the need to communicate. You are the messagener and your message is peace and diplomacy.

If you are born on a number five (overtone) or a number ten (planetary) day, then you are guided by the White Wizard. The enchanter of the Tzolkin. For a White Worldbridger to be guided by enchantment means that you help people cross bridges by enchanting them for their own good.

Note; If you are a White Lunar Worldbridger or a White Electric Worldbridger then you are born on a Portal day. To understand how this affects you please go to the Portal day page. Also it important to discover which wavespell you were born in as this also affects your birth chart. See the wavespell page.
site map contact us

 

 

 




</rich_text>
