            <node unique_id="1157" master_id="0" name="Star_8" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
              <rich_text>Star.8
   Path: \Musing of the Meaning\Humanmetrics\Astrology\Mayan\Yellow\)
Leaf 1:









Yellow Star

The Yellow Star is the eighth glyph and key words associated with it are beauty and elegance. People born on these days literally shine like stars. They have a deep and profound appreciation of all things beautiful. Natural landscapes, fine art, poetry, good food, beautiful people. They see the world as one big shiny sparkly place. Their homes are usually lavishly decorated and colourful. Yellow Stars also take care of their own appearance as well.

All people born on Yellow Star days share in common the same challenge, occult and like minded glyphs in their birth chart. Only the guide changes and that is because the guide is decided by your number.

The challenge for the Yellow Star is the White Mirror. This glyph represents reflecting truth. A challenge is something that makes you stronger, a challenge is given to you as a gift. For if you overcome your challenge, then you have succeed in becoming the strongest person you can become. To have White Mirror as a challenge suggests that people born on Yellow Star days have an issue with the truth. When they look in the mirror either they do not see what is truly there and they suffer from misconceptions or they fail to see their true inner beauty. Perhaps you a star that hides your shining light behind a bushel. Once you have grasped the truth and see the real you the can truly be a star.

The occult glyph for the Yellow Star is the Red Skywalker. This glyph represents courage and exploring. They are the adventurers of the Tzolkin. The occult glyph symbolises your magical gift, you ace up the sleeve. It is the strength you have that protects you. To have the Red Skywalker as a occult glyph means that you are an explorer of magic. You have an open mind and you are willing to explore the world of magic with courage.

The like minded glyph for Yellow Star is the Blue Monkey. The Blue Monkey is all about magic and illusion and play. The like minded glyph is the glyph that has more in common with you than any other in the Tzolkin.. Natural allies, whenever you meet you feel a connection and you make good partnerships.


Day
	

Kin No.
	

Guide
  	  	 
Yellow Magnetic Star
	248 	Yellow Star
Yellow Lunar Star
	28 	Yellow Sun
Yellow Electric Star
	68 	Yellow Human
Yellow Self-existing Star
	108 	Yellow Seed
Yellow Overtone Star
	148 	Yellow Warrior
Yellow Rhythmic Star
	188 	Yellow Star
Yellow Resonant Star
	228 	Yellow Sun
Yellow Galactic Star
	8 	Yellow Human
Yellow Solar Star
	48 	Yellow Seed
Yellow Planetary Star
	88 	Yellow Warrior
Yellow Spectral Star
	128 	Yellow Star
Yellow Crystal Star
	168 	Yellow Sun
Yellow Cosmic Star
	208 	Yellow Human

If you are born on a number one (magnetic) or a number six (rhythmic) or a number eleven (spectral) day, then you are guided by the Yellow Star. You are guided by your own power doubled. People who are guided by themselves are resourceful, self- reliant and often stubborn . Because they are guided by themselves they seldom listen to other people.

If you are born on a number two (lunar) or a number seven (resonant) or a number twelve (crystal) , then you are guided by the
Yellow Sun. This glyph symbolises `enlightenment and universal fire.` To have this as a guiding influence suggests that you are motivated by the search for enlightenment. For you the answer to life on earth is simple. We need only to appreciate the beauty of this planet on the same profound level as the Yellow Star, to find inner peace.

If you are born on a number three (electric) day or a number eight (galactic) or a number thirteen (cosmic), then you are guided by the Yellow Human. This glyph represents `free will, wisdom and channelling`. It is the psychic of the Tzolkin. For a Yellow Star to be guided by Yellow Human suggests that you are guided by your intuition. Channelling messages from spirit is a gift you have and this is a beautiful thing.

If you are born on a number four (self-existing) or a number nine (solar) then you are guided by the Yellow Seed. The Yellow Seed represents sowing awareness. They are spiritual gardeners of the Tzolkin. To be guided by the Yellow Seed entails being guided by the desire to sow awareness in everyone about the beauty of the world we live in.

If you are born on a number five (overtone) or a number ten (planetary), then you are guided by the Yellow Warrior. This glyph represents `questing and intelligence`. To have this as a guiding influence means that you are always on a quest always asking questions.
For Yellow Star guided by Yellow Warriors, life a quest for beauty.

Note. If you are a Yellow Self-Existing Star, Yellow Overtone Star, Yellow Planetary Star or Yellow Crystal Star then you are born on a Portal day.To find out how this affects you please see the Portal day page. Also it is important to take into consideration the wavespell you were born in as this too affects your birth chart. See the wavespell page
