          <node unique_id="1121" master_id="0" name="Astrological Age" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
            <rich_text>Astrological Age
   Path: \Musing of the Meaning\Humanmetrics\Astrology\Western Zodiac\)
Leaf 1:
Astrological ages occur because of a phenomenon known as the precession of the equinoxes. One complete period of this precession is called a Great Sidereal Year of about 25,800 to 25,920 years and it is divided in twelve astrological ages of 30 degrees each (ca. 2150 to 2160 years).

we are currently in the age of pisces and we are approaching the age of aquarius

an age should last approximately 2150 to 2160 years
does this correspond to anything that mayans studied?

The procession of the equinox lasts approx 25,800 - 26.000 years at 365.25 days per year

the mayans believed that we would end our cycle after the 5th age which is howm many times a mayan age goes into the precession of equionoxes

when 26,000 is divided by 13 you get 2,000 years??

the mayan cycle of 5125 
5125 years goes into 26,000 years 5.073170731...

an astrological age goes into the mayan age 2.3837 times

currently accpeted as being 2150-2160 years
I believe that it is actually 2166.66666666667 years as seen when dividing 26,000 by 12

Astrology really has nothing to do with the stars themselves only as a representation of where the sun is at in the sky






</rich_text>
