              <node unique_id="516" master_id="0" name="1564 CE" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
                <node unique_id="517" master_id="0" name="15640423CE" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
                  <rich_text>

April 23, 1564:  The great English dramatist and poet William Shakespeare is born.   Few plays have been performed or analyzed as extensively as the 38 plays ascribed to him, some of the more famous ones being The Taming of the Shrew, Julius Caesar, Richard III, Macbeth, Midsummer Night’s Dream, Henry V, Romeo and Juliet, and Hamlet.  

* </rich_text>
                  <rich_text underline="single">April 23, 1564:</rich_text>
                  <rich_text>  William Shakespeare is born in Stratford-on-Avon.  Although few plays have been performed or analyzed as extensively as the 38 plays ascribed to William Shakespeare, there are few surviving details about his life.  This dearth of biographical information is due primarily to his station in life; he was not a noble, but the son of John Shakespeare, a leather trader and the town bailiff.





</rich_text>
