                <node unique_id="650" master_id="0" name="18511114" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
                  <rich_text>November 14, 1851:  Moby-Dick, a novel by Herman Melville about the voyage of the whaling ship Pequod, is first published.  Moby-Dick is now considered a great classic of American literature and contains one of the most famous opening lines in fiction: "Call me Ishmael."  Initially, though, the book about Captain Ahab and his quest for a giant white whale was a flop.</rich_text>
