                  <rich_text>* March 29, 1973:  Two months after the signing of the Vietnam peace agreement, the last U.S. combat troops leave South Vietnam as Hanoi frees the remaining American prisoners of war held in North Vietnam.  America's direct eight-year intervention in the Vietnam War was at an end. The Vietnam War was the longest and most unpopular foreign war in U.S. history and cost 58,000 American lives.  As many as two million Vietnamese soldiers and civilians were killed.
</rich_text>
