                <node unique_id="941" master_id="0" name="19870612 CE - &quot;Tear Down This Wall&quot;" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
                  <rich_text>
* June 12, 1987:  In one of his most famous Cold War speeches, President Ronald Reagan challenges Soviet Leader Mikhail Gorbachev to tear down the Berlin Wall, a symbol of the Communist era in a divided Germany.  The speech foreshadowed events to come - two years later (9 November, 1989) - joyful East and West Germans did break down the wall, and Germany was officially reunited on October 3, 1990.





</rich_text>
                </node>
