      <node unique_id="1004" master_id="0" name="2000 AD" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="1557537374">
        <rich_text>2000 AD
   Path: \Musing of the Meaning\Time\Known History\)
Leaf 1:






* December 13, 2000:  Vice President Al Gore reluctantly concedes defeat to Texas Governor George W Bush in his bid for the presidency, following weeks of legal battles over the recounting of votes in Florida.  Gore said he had telephoned Bush to offer his congratulations, honoring him, for the first time, with the title ''president-elect.'  ''I promised that I wouldn't call him back this time'' Gore said, referring to the moment on election night when he had called Bush to tell him he was going to concede, then called back a half hour later to retract that concession.
* December 17, 1843:  Charles Dickens A Christmas Carol is published.
* December 17, 1903:  Near Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, Orville and Wilbur Wright make the first successful flight in history of a self-propelled, heavier-than-air aircraft.  The gasoline-powered, propeller-driven biplane stayed aloft for 12 seconds and covered 120 feet on its inaugural flight.  BTW, which brother flew that first plane?  Answer below.

Thats all for this week.



Answer:  Orville piloted the first flight, winning that honor because of a coin toss, if I remember correctly.



</rich_text>
