          <node unique_id="1010" master_id="0" name="2001 AD" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
            <rich_text>2001 AD
   Path: \Musing of the Meaning\Time\Known History\2000 AD\)
Leaf 1:




* November 16, 2001:  British author J.K. Rowlings Harry Potter and the Sorcerers Stone, opens in movie theaters across the U.S.  The first Harry Potter book, Harry Potter and the Philosophers Stone, debuted in Great Britain in 1997 and was released in the United States the following year under the name Harry Potter and the Sorcerers Stone.  To date, the Harry Potter films are the most financially successful series in history, having surpassed both the Star Wars and James Bond franchises.



</rich_text>
            <node unique_id="1014" master_id="0" name="11302001" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="0" ts_lastsave="0">
              <rich_text>
